      "summary": "The reset endpoint checks session and run ownership, and the tests cover reset isolation, audit preservation, evaluator isolation, and fallback metadata. An existing target run ID still escapes as an unhandled exception at the API boundary.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "minor",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Runs/DemoRunResetEndpoints.cs",
          "line": 24,
          "message": "Handle an existing new run ID at the endpoint so an ID collision returns a controlled client error instead of an unhandled server error.",
          "confidence": 0.96,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The endpoint calls reset.Reset, which calls CaseStateStore.CreateCase. The tests show that CreateCase throws InvalidOperationException when the requested new run ID already exists; the endpoint catches CaseAccessDeniedException and DemoRunResetException but not InvalidOperationException.",
            "failureScenario": "If a client retries with a newRunId that another run already uses, the request reaches CreateCase and the endpoint returns an unhandled server error instead of a conflict response."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
